      "writtenOn": "2026-04-20T23:15:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think they are both correct. `ractl.max_index` is an inclusive end of range, while `end` is an exclusive end of range, so a difference of 1 is expected.\n\nI made `ractl.max_index` inclusive so that the default value can be valid value of `ULONG_MAX` instead of a special sentinel value. The pre-existing `limit` and `end_index` variables in readahead.c are also inclusive.\n\n(Confusingly, in this file, there are some variables named like inclusive ends, but aren\u0027t! For example, `last_index` in `filemap_get_pages` that was off by one until https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20230208022400.28962-1-coolqyj@163.com)",
